# React Router docs

When adding or changing routes, navigation, links, loaders, actions, or router setup.

## Version source of truth

1. Read `react-router-dom` from `@package.json` before relying on API details.
2. Use official docs: `https://reactrouter.com/home` (and linked reactrouter.com pages) for the installed major (baseline hint: **7**).
3. Before non-trivial routing, data APIs, or upgrades: open the docs — do not invent patterns from older majors (e.g. v5 / early v6).
4. Cite concrete doc page URLs when recommending APIs, route shapes, or navigation patterns.

## Preferences

- Prefer current React Router APIs documented for this project's version; do not suggest deprecated APIs from older majors without verifying they still apply.
- Follow existing router conventions in this project (`src/app` routes) when present; extend them instead of introducing a parallel router.
- When docs and training knowledge conflict, the official React Router docs for this major win.
